    "family_reading": {
        "text": "Thinking Machines Inkling is a small family of two open weight models, both released in July 2026, both supporting reasoning, and both accepting audio, image and text input while returning text. The context window is 524288 tokens across the family, with a maximum output of 262144 tokens, which suits long documents, large codebases or extended audio and image analysis in one pass. Pricing is modest at the low end, from $0.45 per million input and $1.2 per million output for Inkling Small, rising to $0.95 and $4.05 for the larger Inkling. The limits are that output is text only, so no image or audio generation, and the higher tier costs roughly double on input and over three times on output. No benchmark rows are given, so raw quality is unverified.",
